To build Perkeep:

1) Install Go 1.19 or later.

2) cd to the root of the Perkeep source (where this file is)

3) Run:

   $ go run make.go

4) The compiled binaries should now be in the usual go install directory:
   perkeepd (the server), pk, pk-put, pk-get, and pk-import-runkeeper.

   The build also installs pk-copy-storage (pk-copy-storage.cmd on Windows),
   a tiny wrapper for "perkeepd admin copy-storage", alongside perkeepd.
   It is not a Go program; see cmd/pk-copy-storage/README.md for installation
   without make.go.
